msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:35
msgid "pify(input, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:37
msgid "Returns a `Promise` wrapped version of the supplied function or module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:39
msgid "input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:41
msgid "Type: `Function` `Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:43
msgid "Callback-style function or module whose methods you want to promisify."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:45
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:47
msgid "multiArgs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:49 ../../source/pify_readme.md:78
msgid "Type: `boolean`<br> Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:52
msgid ""
"By default, the promisified function will only return the second argument"
" from the callback, which works fine for most APIs. This option can be "
"useful for modules like `request` that return multiple arguments. Turning"
" this on will make it return an array of all arguments from the callback,"
" excluding the error argument, instead of just the second argument. This "
"also applies to rejections, where it returns an array of all the callback"
" arguments, including the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:63
msgid "include"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:65
msgid "Type: `string[]` `RegExp[]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:67
msgid ""
"Methods in a module to promisify. Remaining methods will be left "
"untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:69
msgid "exclude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:71
msgid "Type: `string[]` `RegExp[]`<br> Default: `[/.+(Sync|Stream)$/]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:74
msgid ""
"Methods in a module **not** to promisify. Methods with names ending with "
"`'Sync'` are excluded by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:76
msgid "excludeMain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:81
msgid ""
"If given module is a function itself, it will be promisified. Turn this "
"option on if you want to promisify only methods of the module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:106
msgid "errorFirst"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:108
msgid "Type: `boolean`<br> Default: `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:111
msgid ""
"Whether the callback has an error as the first argument. You'll want to "
"set this to `false` if you're dealing with an API that doesn't have an "
"error as the first argument, like `fs.exists()`, some browser APIs, "
"Chrome Extension APIs, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:113
msgid "promiseModule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:115
msgid "Type: `Function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:117
msgid "Custom promise module to use instead of the native one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pify_readme.md:119
msgid ""
"Check out [`pinkie-promise`](https://github.com/floatdrop/pinkie-promise)"
" if you need a tiny promise polyfill."
msgstr ""

